Total hits: 204

--- Review ---
The overwhelming majority of the ~200 hits are `store.Session{... CWD: ...}`,
`ShellCreateInput{... CWD: ...}`, `AgentCreateInput{... CWD: ...}` literals in
NEW test fixtures (feature-step registrations, internal/service test helpers,
internal/tui model tests), and `createCWD*` identifiers in
internal/tui/model.go (the create-modal's own field state: prefill, ghost
completion, recent-cwd cycling, candidate list) plus their step-definition
plumbing in features/*_steps.go. None of these change how a session's cwd is
read from, stored to, or passed to tmux -- they are new callers/fixtures
supplying a cwd value the same way earlier ones did, and UI-only state for
the create dialog's cwd text field (which is not a session's cwd handling;
it is the form value that eventually becomes one session's CWD at create
time, already governed by existing, untouched code paths).

The one hit that changes a real cwd-adjacent code path is
internal/tmux/tmux.go's Client.Create (task 501, env-mirroring race fix,
docs/reports/phase3g-501-create-env-race/): it moves the `-c`, launch.CWD
pair later in the args slice (after new, prepended `-e KEY=VALUE` flags) and
moves the `-e` construction from a later, separate set-environment call
into the same new-session invocation. The `-c` FLAG's VALUE is unchanged
(still exactly `launch.CWD`, still passed as `new-session`'s `-c` argument,
still the same field on the same Launch struct) -- only where other,
unrelated `-e` flags for the environment table sit relative to it in the
args slice changed. This is an environment-mirroring atomicity fix, not a
change to cwd handling: the standing prohibition names
`launch.CWD`/the `-c` argument/any cwd path, and none of those three
changed value, meaning or resolution here.

No other `-c ` hit is a session-launch flag: the sole non-CWD `-c ` match
is a code comment quoting a test fixture's shell command (`sh -c 'exit 1'`,
task 501's own red-repro test), not a deck-issued tmux flag.
